    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (d) Liquid HCl</strong></p><p>Hydrogen bonding requires H bonded to highly electronegative and small atoms (F, O, N). Cl is electronegative but too large for effective hydrogen bonding. Phenol ($O{-}H$), $NH_3$ ($N{-}H$), and water ($O{-}H$) all form strong hydrogen bonds.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "year": 1983,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
