    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (c) MnO</strong></p><p>By Fajan's rules, ionic character increases with: (i) low cation charge, (ii) large cation size, (iii) small anion. In MnO, Mn is in +2 oxidation state (lowest among given options), giving least polarizing power → most ionic. $P_2O_5$, $CrO_3$, $Mn_2O_7$ have metals in high oxidation states → more covalent.</p>",
