    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b)</strong></p><p>The least stable ion is one that has the most unfavorable electronic configuration — either violating the octet rule, having too many electrons in antibonding orbitals, or having high charge density on a large atom.</p>",
