    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a, b, d)</strong></p><p>(a) Ice floats: H-bonds create open hexagonal lattice → ice less dense than water ✓. (b) Primary amines more basic in water: better H-bond stabilization of conjugate acid ✓. (c) Formic acid more acidic: due to inductive effect of $CH_3$, not H-bonding ✗. (d) Acetic acid dimerizes via cyclic H-bonds in benzene ✓.</p>",
