    "chapter": "Chemical Bonding And Molecular Structure",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b, c, d)</strong></p><p>(a) $O_2$ is chemisorbed (not physisorbed) since electron transfer occurs ✗. (b) Chemisorption is exothermic → heat released ✓. (c) Electrons transfer from metal to $\\pi^*2p$ of $O_2$ → occupancy increases ✓. (d) More $\\pi^*$ electrons → lower bond order → longer $O{-}O$ bond ✓.</p>",
