    "chapter": "Chemical Bonding And Molecular Structure",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a, d)</strong></p><p>Head-on overlap of two $2p_z$ orbitals forms $\\sigma_{2p}$ (bonding) and $\\sigma^*_{2p}$ (antibonding) molecular orbitals. The bonding MO has electron density concentrated between nuclei, while antibonding has a nodal plane between nuclei.</p>",
