    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: Banana bonds (3-centre-2-electron bonds)</strong></p><p>$B_2H_6$ (diborane) has 4 terminal $B{-}H$ covalent bonds and 2 bridging $B{-}H{-}B$ bonds. The bridging bonds are 3-centre-2-electron (3c-2e) bonds, also called banana bonds or tau bonds, where one pair of electrons is shared among three atoms.</p>",
