    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: Increases, Decreases</strong></p><p>$N_2 \\to N_2^+$: Removing a bonding electron decreases bond order from 3 to 2.5 → bond length increases. $O_2 \\to O_2^+$: Removing an antibonding ($\\pi^*$) electron increases bond order from 2 to 2.5 → bond length decreases.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
