    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: $N_2O$ and $I_3^-$</strong></p><p>$N_2O$: Central N is $sp$ hybridized, linear geometry ($180°$, 16 valence electrons). $I_3^-$: Central I has 3 lone pairs + 2 bond pairs → $sp^3d$ → linear molecular geometry (lone pairs in equatorial positions). $SO_2$ is bent and $I_2^+$ has different geometry.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
