    "options": [],
    "correct": "Check Answer Key",
    "chapter": "Chemical Bonding And Molecular Structure",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>(i) $O_2^{2-}$: $[:O{-}O:]^{2-}$ — isoelectronic neutral molecule: $F_2$ ($[:F{-}F:]$)</p><p>(ii) $CO_3^{2-}$: Trigonal planar with 3 resonance structures — isoelectronic neutral molecule: $SO_3$</p><p>(iii) $CN^-$: $[:C{\\equiv}N:]^-$ — isoelectronic neutral molecule: $N_2$ ($:N{\\equiv}N:$)</p><p>(iv) $NCS^-$: $[:N{=}C{=}S:]^-$ (linear) — isoelectronic neutral molecule: $CO_2$ or $N_2O$</p>",
