    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>Resonance structures of $N_2O$ satisfying octet rule:</p><p>Structure 1: $:N{=}N{=}O:$ (all atoms have 8 electrons)</p><p>Structure 2: $:N{\\equiv}N{-}\\ddot{O}:$ with formal charges ($N^-$, $N^+$, $O^-$)</p><p>Structure 3: $:\\ddot{N}{-}N{\\equiv}O:$ with formal charges ($N^{2-}$, $N^+$, $O^0$)</p><p>All structures maintain octets on each atom. Structure 1 is the most significant contributor.</p>",
