    "number": "89",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "Using the VSEPR theory, identify the type of hybridisation and draw the structure of ${OF}_{2}$ . What are the oxidation states of O and F ?",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "-1, +2",
    "chapter": "Chemical Bonding And Molecular Structure",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: O = +2, F = −1</strong></p><p><strong>Hybridization:</strong> O is central atom with 2 bond pairs ($O{-}F$) + 2 lone pairs = 4 electron domains → $sp^3$ hybridization → bent/V-shaped geometry.</p><p><strong>Oxidation states:</strong> In $OF_2$, fluorine is more electronegative than oxygen. F always takes −1 oxidation state. For $OF_2$: $x + 2(-1) = 0$ → $x = +2$. So O = +2, F = −1.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "year": 1994,
