    "chapter": "Chemical Bonding And Molecular Structure",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: $V^{4+}$: $1s^2\\ 2s^2\\ 2p^6\\ 3s^2\\ 3p^6\\ 3d^1$</strong></p><p>$\\mu = 1.73$ BM $= \\sqrt{n(n+2)}$ where $n$ = number of unpaired electrons. $\\sqrt{1(1+2)} = \\sqrt{3} = 1.73$. So $n = 1$ unpaired electron.</p><p>V (Z=23): $[Ar]\\ 3d^3\\ 4s^2$. To get 1 unpaired electron: $V^{4+}$ loses 4 electrons → $[Ar]\\ 3d^1$ → 1 unpaired electron ✓</p>",
