    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p><strong>ortho-Hydroxybenzaldehyde:</strong> The $-OH$ and $-CHO$ groups are adjacent. Intramolecular hydrogen bond forms between $O{-}H$ (of phenol) and $C{=}O$ (of aldehyde). This reduces intermolecular H-bonding → weaker intermolecular forces → lower bp → liquid at room temperature.</p><p><strong>para-Hydroxybenzaldehyde:</strong> The $-OH$ and $-CHO$ groups are far apart. No intramolecular H-bond possible. Only intermolecular H-bonding occurs → strong intermolecular forces → high melting solid.</p>",
