    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: False</strong></p><p>$MgCl_2 \\cdot 6H_2O$ on direct heating does NOT give anhydrous $MgCl_2$. Instead: $MgCl_2 \\cdot 6H_2O \\xrightarrow{heat} Mg(OH)Cl + HCl + 5H_2O → MgO + 2HCl + 6H_2O$. Hydrolysis occurs. To get anhydrous $MgCl_2$, heat in dry HCl atmosphere.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
