    "chapter": "Hydrogen And S-Block Elements",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>(i) $Ca_3(PO_4)_2 + 3SiO_2 + 5C → 3CaSiO_3 + 5CO + 2P$ (heated in electric furnace at 1500°C). The calcium silicate (slag) is removed.</p><p>(ii) Calcium with water: $Ca + 2H_2O → Ca(OH)_2 + H_2↑$ (reacts less vigorously than Na/K due to formation of protective Ca(OH)₂ layer).</p>",
