    "number": "39",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "A $5.0{cm}^{3}$ solution of ${H}_{2}{O}_{2}$ liberates 0.508 g of iodine from an acidified KI solution. Calculate the strength of ${H}_{2}{O}_{2}$ solution in terms of volume strength at STP.",
    "images": [],
    "options": [
      "",
      "",
      "",
      ""
    ],
    "correct": "4.48 \\text{ mL}",
    "chapter": "Hydrogen And S-Block Elements",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 4.48 mL</strong></p><p>$H_2O_2 + 2KI + H_2SO_4 → K_2SO_4 + I_2 + 2H_2O$. Moles of $I_2 = 0.508/254 = 0.002$ mol. Moles of $H_2O_2 = 0.002$ mol (1:1 ratio). $H_2O_2 → H_2O + \\frac{1}{2}O_2$. $O_2$ produced = 0.001 mol. Volume at STP = $0.001 × 22400 = 22.4$ mL from 5 mL solution. Volume strength = 22.4/5 = 4.48.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
