    "id": "jee_adv_chem_hydrogen_and_s_block_elements_42",
    "number": "42",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "To a $25 mL{H}_{2}{O}_{2}$ solution, excess of acidified solution of potassium iodide was added. The iodine liberated required 20 mL of 0.3 N sodium thiosulphate solution. Calculate the volume strength of ${H}_{2}{O}_{2}$ solution.",
    "images": [],
    "options": [
      "",
      "",
      "",
      ""
    ],
    "correct": "1.344",
    "chapter": "Hydrogen And S-Block Elements",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 1.344</strong></p><p>$H_2O_2 + 2KI + H_2SO_4 → K_2SO_4 + I_2 + 2H_2O$. Moles of $Na_2S_2O_3$ = $20 × 0.3/1000 = 0.006$ mol. $I_2 + 2Na_2S_2O_3 → Na_2S_4O_6 + 2NaI$. Moles of $I_2 = 0.003$. Moles of $H_2O_2 = 0.003$. Mass of $H_2O_2 = 0.003 × 34 = 0.102$ g in 25 mL. Strength = $0.102/25 × 1000 = 4.08$ g/L. Volume strength = $4.08 × 5.6/34 = 0.672$... Let me recalculate: Normality = $0.006/0.025 = 0.24N$. Volume strength = $0.24 × 5.6 = 1.344$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
