    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>$H_2O_2$ as oxidizing agent (in alkaline medium): $Fe^{2+} + H_2O_2 → Fe^{3+} + OH^-$ (Fenton's reaction). $H_2O_2 + 2e^- → 2OH^-$.</p><p>$H_2O_2$ as reducing agent (in alkaline medium): $2Fe^{3+} + H_2O_2 + 2OH^- → 2Fe^{2+} + O_2 + 2H_2O$. $H_2O_2 → O_2 + 2H^+ + 2e^-$. This dual nature is because $O$ in $H_2O_2$ has -1 oxidation state (intermediate between -2 in $H_2O$ and 0 in $O_2$).</p>",
