    "number": "1",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "The bond order of individual carbon-carbon bonds in benzene is",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "c",
    "chapter": "Basic Principles Of Organic Chemistry",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions\n (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans:</strong></p><p>Inductive effect: electron withdrawal/donation through σ bonds. -I: $-NO_2, -CN, -COOH, -F, -Cl, -Br, -OR, -OH$. +I: $-CH_3 < -C_2H_5 < -C(CH_3)_3$ (alkyl groups). Effect decreases with distance.</p>",
