    "chapter": "Basic Principles Of Organic Chemistry",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions\n (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans:</strong></p><p>Carbocation stability: 3° > 2° > 1° > CH₃⁺. Stabilized by: +I (alkyl groups), resonance (allylic, benzylic), hyperconjugation. Rearrangements: 1,2-hydride and 1,2-methyl shifts to form more stable carbocation.</p>",
