    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 4</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>1. A peptide is positively charged at pH=7 if it contains basic amino acid side chains (like Lysine or Arginine) that have a pKa > 7.<br/>2. We analyze the substituents $R_1$ and $R_2$ for the nine peptides.<br/>3. The side chain $(CH_2)_4NH_2$ corresponds to Lysine, which is protonated ($-NH_3^+$) at pH 7.<br/>4. Counting the peptides containing at least one basic group without a neutralizing acidic group gives exactly 4 such peptides.</p>",
