    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 5</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>1. Determine the number and type of ionizable groups in the peptide: N-terminus, C-terminus, and side chains.<br/>2. At pH = 2 (highly acidic), basic groups and acidic groups are protonated. Net charge $z_1 = +2$.<br/>3. At pH = 6 (near isoelectric point for neutral peptides), net charge $z_2 = 0$.<br/>4. At pH = 11 (highly basic), acidic and basic groups are deprotonated. Net charge $z_3 = -3$.<br/>5. Absolute values: $|+2| + |0| + |-3| = 5$. Thus, $z_1 + z_2 + z_3 = 5$.</p>",
