    "topic": "(With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans:</strong></p><p>Chlorobenzene: less reactive in SN reactions due to (i) resonance (C-Cl bond has partial double bond character), (ii) sp² carbon (shorter, stronger bond), (iii) destabilization of transition state. Requires harsh conditions: NaOH at 300°C/200 atm (Dow process).</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
