    "correct": "c",
    "chapter": "Atomic Structure",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (c)</strong></p><p>Cathode rays are streams of electrons. They were discovered using discharge tubes. The charge-to-mass ratio ($e/m$) of cathode ray particles is the same regardless of the gas used, proving they are a universal component of all atoms.</p>",
