    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (d)</strong></p><p>Maximum electrons in a shell with principal quantum number $n$ = $2n^2$. For $n=3$: $2(3)^2 = 18$ electrons. These are distributed as $3s^2\\ 3p^6\\ 3d^{10}$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
