    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a)</strong></p><p>Electronic configuration of $Ni$ (Z=28): $[Ar]\\ 3d^8\\ 4s^2$. For $Ni^{2+}$: loses 2 electrons from $4s$ → $[Ar]\\ 3d^8$. The $3d^8$ configuration has 2 unpaired electrons.</p>",
