    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (c)</strong></p><p>For hydrogen atom, the energy of transition determines the wavelength: $\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = R_H \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$. The largest energy transition (smallest wavelength) in a series is from $n=\\infty$ to the lower level.</p>",
