    "id": "jee_adv_chem_atomic_structure_79",
    "number": "79",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "The Schrodinger wave equation for hydrogen atom is ${ψ}_{2s}= \\frac{1}{4 \\sqrt{2\\pi }} {\\left( \\frac{1}{{a}_{0}} \\right)}^{3/2} \\left( 2- \\frac{{r}_{0}}{{a}_{0}} \\right) {e}^{-{r}_{0}/{a}_{0}}$ Where, ${a}_{0}$ is Bohr's radius. If the radial node in $2s$ be at ${r}_{0}$ , then find ${r}_{0}$ in terms of ${a}_{0}$ .",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "r_0 = 2a_0",
    "chapter": "Atomic Structure",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: $r_0 = 2a_0$</strong></p><p>For $\\psi_{2s}$, the radial node occurs where $\\psi = 0$: $2 - r/a_0 = 0 → r = 2a_0$. At $r = 2a_0$, the wave function changes sign. This is the radial node of the $2s$ orbital. The probability density $|\\psi|^2 = 0$ at this point.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
