    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: $6.626 \\times 10^{-35}$ m</strong></p><p>de Broglie wavelength: $\\lambda = h/(mv) = (6.626 \\times 10^{-34})/(0.1 \\times 100) = (6.626 \\times 10^{-34})/10 = 6.626 \\times 10^{-35}$ m. This is incredibly small (undetectable for macroscopic objects), illustrating why wave nature is not observable for everyday objects.</p>",
