    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>Velocity: $v = \\frac{e^2}{2\\epsilon_0 nh} = \\frac{2.18 \\times 10^6}{n}$ m/s. For $n=1$: $v_1 = 2.18 \\times 10^6$ m/s.</p><p>de Broglie wavelength: $\\lambda = h/(m_e v) = (6.626 \\times 10^{-34})/(9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\times 2.18 \\times 10^6) = 3.34 \\times 10^{-10}$ m = $3.34$ Å.</p><p>Also: $2\\pi r_1 = \\lambda$ (one complete wave in first orbit). $r_1 = 0.529$ Å, $2\\pi \\times 0.529 = 3.32$ Å ≈ $\\lambda$. ✓</p>",
