    "correct": "c",
    "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions\n (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b)</strong></p><p>Arrhenius equation: $k = Ae^{-E_a/RT}$. Higher temperature → larger $k$ → faster reaction. $\\ln k = \\ln A - E_a/RT$. Plot of $\\ln k$ vs $1/T$: slope = $-E_a/R$, intercept = $\\ln A$.</p>",
