    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b)</strong></p><p>Given $k$, $E_a$, and $A$ at 25°C: use $k = Ae^{-E_a/RT}$. The pre-exponential factor $A$ represents the frequency of collisions with correct orientation. The rate constant $k$ is always less than $A$ since $e^{-E_a/RT} < 1$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "year": 1996,
