    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions\n (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (d)</strong></p><p>$2N_2O_5 → 4NO_2 + O_2$. $k = 3.0 \\times 10^{-5}$ s⁻¹. Rate of disappearance of $N_2O_5$: $-\\frac{d[N_2O_5]}{dt} = k[N_2O_5]$. Rate of formation of $NO_2 = 2k[N_2O_5]$. Rate of formation of $O_2 = \\frac{k}{2}[N_2O_5]$.</p>",
