    "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>From rate data at different concentrations, determine order w.r.t. A and B. At 27°C: $k_{27} = \\frac{0.693}{t_{1/2}} = \\frac{0.693}{30} = 0.0231$ min⁻¹ (if first order). Using Arrhenius: $\\ln(k_2/k_1) = \\frac{E_a}{R}\\left(\\frac{1}{T_1} - \\frac{1}{T_2}\\right)$. Solve for $E_a = 43.848$ kJ/mol.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
