    "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Model Answer:</strong></p><p>From the graph: (i) At equilibrium, $[B]/[A]$ gives $n$ (since $K = [B]^n_{eq}/[A]_{eq}$). (ii) Initial rate gives $k_f$. (iii) At equilibrium: $K_c = k_f/k_b$. Plot analysis shows $n = 2$, and from concentrations: $K = 1.2$, $[A]_{eq} = 0.1$ mol/L.</p>",
