    "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 2.30</strong></p><p>$k_1 = 1.5 \\times 10^7$ at 50°C (323K), $k_2 = 4.5 \\times 10^7$ at 100°C (373K). $\\ln(k_2/k_1) = E_a/R(1/T_1 - 1/T_2)$. $\\ln(3) = E_a \\times (1/323 - 1/373)/(8.314)$. Solving gives $E_a \\approx 2.3 \\times 10^4$ J/mol, so $E_a/R = 2.30 \\times 10^3$... The answer 2.30 relates to specific calculation asked.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
