    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "At constant temperature and volume, $X$ decomposes as $2{X}_{(g)}⟶3{Y}_{(g)}+2{Z}_{(g)}$ ${P}_{x}$ is the partial pressure of $X$ . <table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:10px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">Observationnumber</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">Time(in minute)</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">${P}_{X}$ (in mm of Hg)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">1</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">0</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">800</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">2</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">100</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">400</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">200</td><td style=\"padding:5px;border:1px solid black;\">200</td></tr></table> (i) What is the order of reaction with respect to $$ ? (ii) Find the rate constant. (iii) Find the time for $75%$ completion of the reaction. (iv) Find the total pressure when pressure of $X$ is 700 mm of Hg .",
