    "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "topic": "Assertion & Reason",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a)</strong></p><p>S1: Temperature coefficient ≈ 2 (rate doubles per 10°C rise) — TRUE. S2: The exponential factor in Arrhenius increases with T — TRUE, and this IS the correct explanation. $k = Ae^{-E_a/RT}$; as T↑, $e^{-E_a/RT}$↑, so $k$↑ approximately 2-3× per 10°C.</p>",
