    "number": "60",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Consider the following reversible reaction, ${A}_{(g)}+{B}_{(g)}⇌A{B}_{(g)}$ The activation energy of the backward reaction exceeds that of the forward reaction by $2RT$ (in $J{mol}^{-1}$ ). If the pre-exponential factor of the forward reaction is 4 times that of the reverse reaction, the absolute value of $\\Delta {G}^{∘}$ (in $J{mol}^{-1}$ ) for the reaction at 300 K is $$ (Given : $ln(2)=0.7,RT=2500 J{mol}^{-1}$ at 300 K and $G$ is the Gibbs energy)",
    "images": [],
