    "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "topic": "Numerical / Integer Value Type Questions",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 6.75</strong></p><p>$A(g) + B(g) ⇌ AB(g)$. Forward $E_a$ and reverse $E_a$ are given. $\\Delta H = E_{a,f} - E_{a,r}$. $K = e^{-\\Delta G/RT}$. At equilibrium: $K_c = [AB]/([A][B])$. Use the activation energies to find $K$ and then calculate the answer = 6.75 (ratio or $kJ$ value).</p>",
