    "chapter": "Solid State",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b)</strong></p><p>FCC: X at lattice sites = 4 atoms. Alternate tetrahedral voids: FCC has 8 tetrahedral voids, alternate = 4. Total atoms = 4 + 4 = 8. Volume of atoms = $8 \\times \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$. For FCC: $a = 2\\sqrt{2}r$. Packing efficiency = $\\frac{8 \\times \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3}{a^3} \\times 100$. With tetrahedral void atoms having smaller radius, calculate accordingly.</p>",
