    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b, c)</strong></p><p>Defects in solids: (b) Schottky defect decreases density (equal cation and anion vacancies) — TRUE. (c) Frenkel defect doesn't change density (ion displaced to interstitial site, no vacancy from crystal) — TRUE. Schottky: NaCl, KCl. Frenkel: AgBr, ZnS (small cation, large anion).</p>",
