    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a)</strong></p><p>Physisorption increases with: (i) increase in pressure (more gas molecules available), (ii) decrease in temperature (lower kinetic energy, gas molecules stay adsorbed longer). Rate of physisorption increases with increase in surface area and pressure of gas.</p>",
