    "chapter": "Surface Chemistry",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a, b, d)</strong></p><p>Correct statements about gas adsorption: (a) Physisorption decreases with increase in temperature — TRUE (weakens van der Waals forces). (b) Physisorption is multilayer while chemisorption is monolayer — TRUE. (d) Chemisorption involves formation of chemical bonds — TRUE. Energy of chemisorption > physisorption.</p>",
